{"slug": "job-quote-estimator", "title": "Free Job Quote Estimator for Field Service (Calculator)", "description": "Free job quote calculator for cleaning, lawn, pool, pest and home service businesses: labor, materials, travel, overhead and target margin.", "h1": "Field service job quote estimator", "keyword": "job quote calculator", "type": "tool", "tools": [], "trades": [], "body": "<style>.calc{display:grid;gap:.6rem;max-width:560px}.calc label{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;align-items:center}.calc input{width:9rem;padding:.35rem}.out{background:#f2f7f5;padding:1rem;border-radius:8px;margin:1rem 0}.out td{padding:.2rem .8rem .2rem 0}.ck li{margin:.35rem 0;list-style:none}.ck input{margin-right:.5rem}@media print{header,footer,.trust,.noprint{display:none}}</style><p>Build a job quote from your own labor, materials, travel and overhead numbers, then set a target profit margin. Runs entirely in your browser. The starting values are placeholders, not industry averages.</p><form class=\"calc\" id=\"c\" onsubmit=\"return false\"><label for=\"h\">Estimated labor hours (per worker)<input id=\"h\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" step=\"any\" value=\"3\"></label><label for=\"w\">Workers on the job<input id=\"w\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" step=\"1\" value=\"2\"></label><label for=\"lr\">Labor cost per worker-hour, incl. payroll costs ($)<input id=\"lr\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" step=\"any\" value=\"25\"></label><label for=\"mat\">Materials and supplies cost ($)<input id=\"mat\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" step=\"any\" value=\"80\"></label><label for=\"mu\">Materials markup (%)<input id=\"mu\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" step=\"any\" value=\"0\"></label><label for=\"mi\">Round-trip miles<input id=\"mi\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" step=\"any\" value=\"20\"></label><label for=\"cpm\">Vehicle cost per mile ($)<input id=\"cpm\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" step=\"any\" value=\"0.7\"></label><label for=\"oh\">Overhead allocation per job ($)<input id=\"oh\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" step=\"any\" value=\"0\"></label><label for=\"mg\">Target profit margin on price (%)<input id=\"mg\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" step=\"any\" value=\"20\"></label><label for=\"tax\">Sales tax on materials (%)<input id=\"tax\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" step=\"any\" value=\"0\"></label></form><div class=\"out\" aria-live=\"polite\"><table id=\"r\"></table></div><p class=\"note\">Margin is not the same as markup: a 20% margin means profit is 20% of the final price (price = cost ÷ (1 − margin)). Formula: cost = labor + materials (with markup and tax) + travel + overhead. Check your own vehicle cost per mile; the default is a placeholder. Need software that turns quotes into jobs? See <a href=\"/compare/jobber-vs-housecall-pro/\">Jobber vs Housecall Pro</a>.</p><script>(function(){var f=document.getElementById('c'),r=document.getElementById('r');function v(i){return parseFloat(document.getElementById(i).value)||0}function $(n){return '$'+n.toLocaleString(undefined,{minimumFractionDigits:2,maximumFractionDigits:2})}\nfunction calc(){var lab=v('h')*v('w')*v('lr'),mat=v('mat')*(1+v('mu')/100)*(1+v('tax')/100),trav=v('mi')*v('cpm'),cost=lab+mat+trav+v('oh'),mg=Math.min(v('mg'),95)/100,price=cost/(1-mg),hrs=v('h')*v('w');\nr.innerHTML='<tr><td>Labor</td><td>'+$(lab)+'</td></tr><tr><td>Materials (with markup and tax)</td><td>'+$(mat)+'</td></tr><tr><td>Travel</td><td>'+$(trav)+'</td></tr><tr><td>Overhead</td><td>'+$(v('oh'))+'</td></tr><tr><td>Total job cost</td><td><b>'+$(cost)+'</b></td></tr><tr><td>Quote price at '+(mg*100).toFixed(0)+'% margin</td><td><b>'+$(price)+'</b></td></tr><tr><td>Profit</td><td>'+$(price-cost)+'</td></tr><tr><td>Effective markup on cost</td><td>'+(cost?((price/cost-1)*100).toFixed(1):'0')+'%</td></tr><tr><td>Revenue per worker-hour</td><td>'+(hrs?$(price/hrs):'n/a')+'</td></tr>'}\nf.addEventListener('input',calc);calc()})();</script>", "faq": [["What's the difference between margin and markup?", "Markup is profit as a percentage of cost; margin is profit as a percentage of price. Pricing a $100 cost at a 20% margin gives $125, which is a 25% markup."], ["Does this estimator use industry rates?", "No. The starting values are placeholders. Enter your own labor cost, vehicle cost and margin."], ["Is anything I enter saved?", "No. Everything is calculated in your browser."]]}